# Privacy & account lifecycle

## Public profile

Only expose fields intended for discovery, such as:
- display name
- profile photo
- country/city at coarse granularity
- languages
- proficiency
- learning goals
- interests
- short bio
- availability

Never expose private account fields through discovery APIs.

## Privacy controls

Support the repository's actual settings model for:
- discovery visibility
- message permissions
- profile visibility
- notification preferences
- online/presence visibility

## Account deletion

Deletion must follow the product's actual retention policy.

Consider:
- anonymizing authored content where required
- removing private profile data
- revoking sessions/tokens
- disabling discovery
- deactivating device tokens
- handling conversations and reports consistently

Do not implement destructive deletion casually without checking existing data-retention requirements.
